VulDB Recent.description:
A vulnerability identified as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">very critical</a> has been detected in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/trendnet:tew-657brm">TRENDnet TEW-657BRM 1.00.1</a>. This issue affects some unknown processing of the file <em>/usr/sbin/upgrade_flash.cgi</em>. Performing a manipulation of the argument <em>boundary</em> results in stack-based buffer overflow.

This vulnerability is reported as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-129352">CVE-2026-129352</a>. The attack is possible to be carried out remotely. Moreover, an exploit is present.

The vendor explains: &quot;&quot;I am not able to confirm if such vulnerability exists as the product has been EOL for more than 15 years. We will send out an announcement letting customers know.&quot;

A vulnerability categorized as <a href="https://vuldb.com/kb/risk">very critical</a> has been discovered in <a href="https://vuldb.com/product/trendnet:tew-657brm">TRENDnet TEW-657BRM 1.00.1</a>. This vulnerability affects the function <code>sprintf</code> of the file <em>/setup.cgi</em> of the component <em>mini_httpd</em>. Such manipulation leads to out-of-bounds write. This vulnerability only affects products that are no longer supported by the maintainer.

This vulnerability is documented as <a href="https://vuldb.com/cve/CVE-2026-129351">CVE-2026-129351</a>. The attack can be executed remotely. Additionally, an exploit exists.

The vendor explains: &quot;&quot;I am not able to confirm if such vulnerability exists as the product has been EOL for more than 15 years. We will send out an announcement letting customers know.&quot;
